I acknowledge how compelling this argument looks in practice as well – particularly focusing on local vs external pressures affecting wage decisions made by export-oriented firms whose operations hinge heavily on global supply chains and price fluctuations abroad, thereby tempering expectations about artificially inflating employee salaries under circumstances governed strongly by unforgiving commercial environments worldwide, implying structural barriers standing behind stubborn realities resisting idealistic predictions.

